## 5. Final Recommendation

If you want the absolute largest step-change reduction in MAE, you must abandon tabular regression and execute **Direction 1 combined with Direction 3**: 

**Deploy an Earth Observation Foundation Model (Presto or SatMAE) utilizing a Sequence-to-Sequence Change Point Detection formulation.**

1. **Why?** It attacks the two largest bottlenecks simultaneously. The Foundation Model reconstructs the cloud-masked optical data using learned Earth physics, bypassing the sensor limits. The Change Point formulation stops penalizing the model for continuous variance and focuses it purely on detecting the discrete structural break in the vegetation signal.
2. **Implementation:** We will discard `step_06` (manual features) entirely. We will feed raw, multi-band, temporally-stamped pixels into the Foundation Model encoder, and train a lightweight decoder to output a temporal probability mask of the harvest event.
3. **Development Time:** ~1-2 weeks. Requires massive GPU memory to fine-tune the transformer, and a complete rewrite of the data loading pipeline to support raw temporal pixel arrays instead of aggregated tabular statistics.
